<!-- Source of docs/assets/scanner-update-flow.svg. Export and cleanup: docs/assets/src/README.md -->
<mxfile host="drawio" agent="hand-authored" version="30.0.4">
  <diagram id="scanner-update-flow" name="Scanner updates"
           figure-title="Scanner updates: on a schedule, proven, reviewed"
           figure-desc="Flow of the weekly scanner pin update. Every Monday at 02:17 UTC, or on a manual run, the update-pins workflow runs update_pins.py --check, which asks Docker Hub and GHCR anonymously for each scanner's newest stable tag and the digest of its multi-arch image index; a tag is proposed only after it has been public for 7 days, and never as a downgrade. Exit 0 means every pin is current and the run ends quietly. Otherwise smoke_scanners.py runs each candidate image on a fixture with one planted defect per scanner, eight scanners, and the image must still find it; this job holds only a read token, so new images never see the write token. update_pins.py --write then moves the pins in both editions and the gates run: both selftests, the offline eval, edition parity, plugin manifests, numbers and versions. The result is one pull request from bot/scanner-pins, labelled scanner-pins, with release-notes links, a draft CHANGELOG entry and the smoke-test table; CI runs on three operating systems. A maintainer reviews and merges it by hand, it is never auto-merged, and a z release ships the new pins. If the lookup, the smoke test, a gate or the pull request step fails, one issue &quot;update-pins failed&quot; is opened, later failures comment on it, and the next successful run closes it. During an audit the pins never move: images are fixed by digest and the Phase 8 re-scan uses the same rules; run_scanners.py --check-updates only reports newer versions, never pulls or changes a pin, and --pin tries one version on purpose.">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1260" dy="820" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="0" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1260" pageHeight="820" math="0" shadow="0" background="none">
